publisher.jar
# IG Publisher build artifacts (java -jar publisher.jar -ig . -tx n/a - see README/install-to-cache.sh)
output/
temp/
template/
input-cache/
Requirements-fromNarrative.json
# IG Publisher's own build-time cache/index files inside local-template/ -
# not source, regenerated on every build.
local-template/**/.index.json
local-template/**/.index.db
# Test Case pages (input/pagecontent/au-core-*.md, au-imagingresult.md) generated by
# fhir-frog-testscript-render's TestScriptRenderCli from input/resources/ are committed to
# git, not ignored - HL7's build.fhir.org auto-builder clones this repo directly and runs
# the IG Publisher with no knowledge of our custom CI generation step, so sushi-config.yaml's
# pages: block needs these files to actually exist in git (see commit history: same lesson as
# 4c0d9b9's SUSHI fsh-generated output fix). The GitLab CI "build" job's before_script still
# regenerates them fresh on every run so local dev/CI can diff against the committed copies and
# catch drift - see .gitlab-ci.yml and README.md's "Build" section to run the same CLI locally.
